Subject: cmd/link, runtime: build no findfunctab on wasm
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

findfunctab maps a PC to its ftab entry through one bucket per 4096
bytes of program counter. A wasm PC is the function index shifted left
by 16, so every function owned sixteen buckets whether it had one
instruction or a thousand, and the table grew with the number of
functions to a large share of a program's data, most of it zero and all
of it written into memory at start. On wasm the index of a function's
ftab entry is the function's index within the text for every function
with an entry of its own, so findfunc now indexes ftab directly and
falls back to a binary search over the sorted entries where a container
symbol has shifted them; the linker emits an empty table.

